  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sri Kodisi Kishore Raja vs The State Of Andhra Pradesh on 12 September, 2019 Honourable Sri Justice D.V.S.S. Somayajulu Writ Petition No.13393 of 2019 O R D E R:",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "2) Heard, Sri Y.N. Anjaneyacharyulu, learned counsel for the petitioner who argued that his client is being prosecuted twice for the same offence. Learned Government Pleader opposes the same stating that parallel proceedings can continue and that the law on the subject is very clear. He submits that 5th respondent can impose penalty. It is also the contention of the learned Government Pleader that the standard of proof and the quality of evidence in these two proceedings are different, and, therefore, 'double jeopardy, etc., will not apply and that the acquittal in the criminal case will not bar the respondent No.5 from entertaining or disposing the case before him.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "2) Heard, Sri Y.N. Anjaneyacharyulu, learned counsel for the petitioner who argued that his client is being prosecuted twice for the same offence. Learned Government Pleader opposes the same stating that parallel proceedings can continue and that the law on the subject is very clear. He submits that 5th respondent can impose penalty. It is also the contention of the learned Government Pleader that the standard of proof and the quality of evidence in these two proceedings are different, and, therefore, 'double jeopardy, etc., will not apply and that the acquittal in the criminal case will not bar the respondent No.5 from entertaining or disposing the case before him.",
